WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.381
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.810
NARRATOR: Eat one of these and
you'll be sure to find yourself

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.630
in a sticky situation,
but no worries,

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:14.120
it's all ooey gooey fun.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.610
A sticky bun is all
about messy eating.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:20.180
Consuming one is a lip-smacking,
finger-licking experience.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:21.560
No utensils required.

00:00:24.896 --> 00:00:27.820
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.100
Sticky buns are sometimes
called schnecken

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.500
due to their German origins.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.900
Schnecken is the
German word for snails,

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.600
which the cinnamon
swirl on top resembles.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.035
They start with
all-purpose flour.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.230
Then blend in a premix of
sugar, salt, and baking powder.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
Cream cheese and
butter come next.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.300
These fats are just
the right consistency

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.730
for an automated dough
hook to efficiently work

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.500
them into the dry ingredients.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:01.030
An employee then pours
milk into the blender.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:03.010
It binds the
ingredients, turning

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.019
the mix into biscuit dough.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:08.270
The dough needs to stay cool
for food safety reasons,

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:09.890
so they monitor the temperature.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.290
The next worker loads the
dough into an extruder

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.660
that squeezes it into
a wide flat strip

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:17.605
called the dough band.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.070
The dough band rides
a conveyor that slopes

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.470
down to a narrow channel.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.450
As it enters, the dough
folds over from the sides,

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.445
creating two layers.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.120
A roller squeezes
the layers thinner.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.890
A device called the fanner now
zigzags back and forth to layer

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.925
the dough ribbon style.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:42.300
The layers pile up six deep.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.850
And because they were
originally two layers,

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.485
there are now 12 in total.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.060
Metal rollers press the
pack down and thin it

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.895
substantially until it's
about 2/10 of an inch thick.

00:01:53.895 --> 00:01:56.904
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.670
Next up is the
sticky bun filling

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.440
called cinnamon schmear.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.650
It starts with blocks of butter
and lots of ground cinnamon.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.639
They add brown sugar
instead of white.

00:02:10.639 --> 00:02:13.380
It has an intense molasses
flavor and a stickier

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.180
than white sugar.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:20.040
Canola oil loosens and
homogenizes the ingredients,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.470
transforming the mix
into the sugary cinnamon

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.090
paste known as the schmear.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.690
This cinnamon schmear is the
consistency of cake frosting,

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.940
so it can be easily
pumped over to the dough.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.072
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.430
A series of nozzles deposit
dollops of the cinnamon

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.035
smear onto the sticky bun dough.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.280
The dough travels under
a long blade that spreads

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.600
the cinnamon schmear evenly.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.950
A device called a plough
then lifts the outside edges

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:52.940
and folds them over.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:57.770
Rollers press down the
curled edges to tighten them.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:00.380
Each tightly curled edge
will now become the center

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.445
of a sticky bun roll.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.510
Angled rollers
called roll winders

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.340
pick up the curled
edges of the dough

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.905
and fold it into two
parallel cinnamon rolls.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:16.340
A guillotine blade slices
the parallel rolls into buns,

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.570
creating sets of two.

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.700
Meanwhile, the sweet
and sticky topping is

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:24.830
bubbling away in a big kettle.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:28.350
It's made of honey,
brown sugar, and butter.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.350
This topping actually
goes on the bottom

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:32.210
onto the baking tray.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:35.270
They pump it into the container
and then toss in pecans

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.125
to give it some crunch.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.490
Putting the topping on the
bottom of the baking tray

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.530
means, of course,
that these sticky buns

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.875
are to be baked upside down
once purchased by the consumer.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:50.780
It's a strategic
baking technique.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.780
Cooked upside down, the
sticky topping will saturate

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.145
the buns for added moisture.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.830
And by not exposing the
topping to direct heat,

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.920
it won't burn as it caramelizes
into a sugary glaze.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.298
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.200
The sticky buns.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.680
Now head into a tunnel
chilled by liquid nitrogen

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.230
for a very fast freeze.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.890
After about four minutes,
the buns emerge frozen solid,

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.600
with the freshness locked in.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.500
The sticky buns then
ride another conveyor

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.120
to the wrapping station.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.730
Here, machinery quickly
seals plastic film

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:36.860
around each box of buns, after
which it's sent to an oven

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.990
to heat shrink the plastic.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:42.140
It all happens in seconds,
giving the frozen buns

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.235
no time to thaw.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.810
It has taken hours of
prep work at the factory,

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:50.390
but these frozen sticky
buns are ready for baking.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:54.620
All the cook has to do is
pop the tray in the oven,

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:57.620
and the buns will be
ready in 20 minutes.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.800
No need to get your hands sticky
by making them from scratch.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.150
[MUSIC PLAYING]

